{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1274301-are-there-any-new-original-settings-planed-for-trinity","id":1274301,"title":"Are there any new original settings planed for Trinity?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-12-13T21:28:48-08:00","id":1274301,"title":"Are there any new original settings planed for Trinity?","content":"I'd love to see a full blown space opera using the Storypath system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-13T23:46:41-08:00","id":1274319,"title":"","content":"At the moment, we know of two - Anima (post-Aberrant War braintech-heavy cyberpunk) and Aegis (Classical Mythology).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-14T04:20:55-08:00","id":1274341,"title":"","content":"And it suddenly dawned on me that all the setting's names start with an A, on purpose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-14T10:23:22-08:00","id":1274385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jeremysbrain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1274301-are-there-any-new-original-settings-planed-for-trinity?p=1274341#post1274341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And it suddenly dawned on me that all the setting's names start with an A, on purpose.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hohoho yeah it\u2019s been so long since everyone was in on the alliteration that I chuckle seeing someone just discover it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-14T11:15:30-08:00","id":1274399,"title":"","content":"I too would love a post-Aeon space opera game. But we are years away from getting one announced, even if there are related ideas jotted down in Ian's notebook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1897-ffanxii4ever","name":"ffanxii4ever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-15T04:20:15-08:00","id":1274540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ffanxii4ever</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1274301-are-there-any-new-original-settings-planed-for-trinity?p=1274399#post1274399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I too would love a post-Aeon space opera game. But we are years away from getting one announced, even if there are related ideas jotted down in Ian's notebook.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I believe Ian has stated in the past that he's got many time periods planned and a space opera long after \u00c6on is one of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=485\" data-tempid=\"temp_485_1538393298974_786\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1277-karpomatic","name":"karpomatic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1277_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"143"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-15T11:13:47-08:00","id":1274593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>karpomatic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1274301-are-there-any-new-original-settings-planed-for-trinity?p=1274540#post1274540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I believe Ian has stated in the past that he's got many time periods planned and a space opera long after \u00c6on is one of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>gosh that\u2019s actually top on my list for most desired eras!<br /> <br /> I think I heard it was not set to come out anytime soon though. But it could support all era level characters and any type of world!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-17T11:32:49-08:00","id":1274913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1274301-are-there-any-new-original-settings-planed-for-trinity?p=1274385#post1274385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hohoho yeah it\u2019s been so long since everyone was in on the alliteration that I chuckle seeing someone just discover it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's amusing to me that the books lasted so much longer than the show MTV flexed its muscles over.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-17T11:41:21-08:00","id":1274918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1274301-are-there-any-new-original-settings-planed-for-trinity?p=1274913#post1274913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's amusing to me that the books lasted so much longer than the show MTV flexed its muscles over.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah Aeon Flux! Haha yeah I hate having to compromise something due to corporate trademarked naming. Like when they called it the Mothman even though people were describing it as a bat but they didn\u2019t want to get hassled by the Adam West show at the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-23T14:30:46-08:00","id":1276322,"title":"","content":"Is there any information available right now on the Aegis setting? If so, could I have a link please?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-26T02:41:18-08:00","id":1276770,"title":"","content":"As far as I know, nothing's been really detailed about it anywhere other than it's supposed to play with the whole &quot;What if the ancient gods were actually Novas&quot; premise. I imagine we'll hear more about it once Aberrant is further along (at the earliest).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Christopher Shaffer, freelancer. Game line contributions: W20, Night Horrors, TC: \u00c6on, Scion (details <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2019/07/stuff-ive-worked-on.html\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>) <br /> <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2020/10/actual-play-index.html\" target=\"_blank\"> <b>Blog post write-ups of my gaming sessions; Currently running Exalted, and also updating old Promethean sessions</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/171-mythicfox","name":"MythicFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar171_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-26T11:45:15-08:00","id":1276842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MythicFox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1274301-are-there-any-new-original-settings-planed-for-trinity?p=1276770#post1276770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as I know, nothing's been really detailed about it anywhere other than it's supposed to play with the whole &quot;What if the ancient gods were actually Novas&quot; premise. I imagine we'll hear more about it once Aberrant is further along (at the earliest).</div> </div> </div> </div>Kinda seems like a perfect Scion setting but it's probably fine as a Trinity one too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-26T13:10:48-08:00","id":1276852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aristarkos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1274301-are-there-any-new-original-settings-planed-for-trinity?p=1276842#post1276842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Kinda seems like a perfect Scion setting but it's probably fine as a Trinity one too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Scion premises and mechanics makes Aegis setting ( with mythic heroes ) implying Aberrant setting coming from our own future impossible. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1274898-everyday-life-with-gods?p=1276360#post1276360\">Had a large discussion how Scion bases makes setting almost impossible to look like our real world, with the same history</a>. ( Warning, you read this topic on your own responsibility. )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-26T23:32:19-08:00","id":1276963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aristarkos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1274301-are-there-any-new-original-settings-planed-for-trinity?p=1276842#post1276842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Kinda seems like a perfect Scion setting but it's probably fine as a Trinity one too.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, for Scion, that would just be, like, a historical setting. The idea of historical Novas being mistaken for deities is probably a little more distinctive in a setting that doesn't already have actual, literal gods running around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Christopher Shaffer, freelancer. Game line contributions: W20, Night Horrors, TC: \u00c6on, Scion (details <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2019/07/stuff-ive-worked-on.html\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>) <br /> <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2020/10/actual-play-index.html\" target=\"_blank\"> <b>Blog post write-ups of my gaming sessions; Currently running Exalted, and also updating old Promethean sessions</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/171-mythicfox","name":"MythicFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar171_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-27T00:38:26-08:00","id":1276969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aristarkos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1274301-are-there-any-new-original-settings-planed-for-trinity?p=1276842#post1276842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Kinda seems like a perfect Scion setting but it's probably fine as a Trinity one too.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, Aegis is about the ancient gods being Novas. That wouldn\u2019t make any sense in a world where the ancient gods are... you know... gods.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-27T09:43:37-08:00","id":1277025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MythicFox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1274301-are-there-any-new-original-settings-planed-for-trinity?p=1276963#post1276963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well, for Scion, that would just be, like, a historical setting. The idea of historical Novas being mistaken for deities is probably a little more distinctive in a setting that doesn't already have actual, literal gods running around.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes I get that and it seems like a fine idea. I hope they explore and present the whole gammut of ancient civilizations from Britain to China rather than just focus on the same old Rome and Greece.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-29T08:59:22-08:00","id":1277367,"title":"","content":"And lets not forgett ancient India with stuff like the Mahabharata. This also should be a great source of Inspiration for a campain about Novas in the ancient world.<br /> By the way - I wonder, how far Aegis will wander into Erich-von-D\u00e4niken-territory. After all, Trinity isnt Scion. Did the Novas of old also come up with weird Super-Science? Was Talos a Cyborg? Were Vimanas Starships? Did some Aliens also pose as gods?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24955-waldi","name":"Waldi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-29T11:17:10-08:00","id":1277380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aristarkos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1274301-are-there-any-new-original-settings-planed-for-trinity?p=1276322#post1276322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there any information available right now on the Aegis setting? If so, could I have a link please?</div> </div> </div> </div>Aegis will apparently feature heroes, wizards, and gods \u2014 that is, Talents, Psiads, and Novas. Think if it more along the lines of Adventure or Aberrant in ancient Greece, depending on how potent the superhumans are. <br /> <br /> Bear in mind, though, that prior to the Hammersmith Event that kicked off Adventure, empowerment events were always local and temporary, and rare. Aegis is unlikely to cover more than the territory of Greece, and is unlikely to last even as long as a century. Don't expect it to get into other ancient cultures. <br /> <br /> Though honestly, I'd rather see Aegis be based around Atlantis instead of Greece, giving a clear ending point to the age \u2014 assuming, of course, that the heroes don't interfere and divert the impending disaster. This is the Continuum, after all; we're not forced into a single timeline. Though even if Atlantis is saved from utter destruction in a single night, it's still likely to succumb to the ravages of time as its gods and sorcerers fade away into the mists of prehistory. <br /> <br /> Of course, there's also the possibility that its ending isn't what it seemed: what if the \u201csinking\u201d of Atlantis was the detonation of a temporal bomb, and the island got shifted forward in time by a few millennia? Say, re-emerging sometime in the 23rd century\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-29T12:31:32-08:00","id":1277387,"title":"","content":"Or maybe, it was not a temporal bomb, but a transdimensional one. So, Atlantis &quot;reapears&quot; everyone now and then, just to be drawn Back again into its own pocket Reality. This could work quite nicely, because &quot;stumbling over Atlantis&quot; could fit in almost any era of Trinity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24955,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24955-waldi","user":"Waldi","date":". 12-29-2018, 04:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24955-waldi","name":"Waldi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-03T13:12:15-08:00","id":1278393,"title":"","content":"Adventures in Atlantis gets a thousand points from me. I would love an Atlantis of talents, psions, and novas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-03T14:12:48-08:00","id":1278412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aristarkos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1274301-are-there-any-new-original-settings-planed-for-trinity?p=1277025#post1277025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes I get that and it seems like a fine idea. I hope they explore and present the whole gammut of ancient civilizations from Britain to China rather than just focus on the same old Rome and Greece.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Personally I prefer the corebook stay focused on only Ancient Greece and Rome... make China and India and the rest of Europe be supplements. Trying to cover everything in the core book just leaves you with a shallow amount of information for play. Give me a setting I can use right out of the box, instead of 2 pages on every single nation-state of the ancient world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3769-orphan81","name":"Orphan81","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3769_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-03T15:17:53-08:00","id":1278430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ffanxii4ever</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1274301-are-there-any-new-original-settings-planed-for-trinity?p=1274399#post1274399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I too would love a post-Aeon space opera game. But we are years away from getting one announced, even if there are related ideas jotted down in Ian's notebook.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Argosy seems like a likely name for a space opera. I like the idea of a Time War that links all the settings and it could be called Agon (struggle). A game with Adventure! type inspired in the 1580-1720 period (Swashers mainly) could be called Anthor ( an Alchemist's furnace).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 01-03-2019, 06:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-12T21:26:26-08:00","id":1280442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Waldi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1274301-are-there-any-new-original-settings-planed-for-trinity?p=1277367#post1277367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And lets not forgett ancient India with stuff like the Mahabharata. This also should be a great source of Inspiration for a campain about Novas in the ancient world.<br /> By the way - I wonder, how far Aegis will wander into Erich-von-D\u00e4niken-territory. After all, Trinity isnt Scion. Did the Novas of old also come up with weird Super-Science? Was Talos a Cyborg? Were Vimanas Starships? Did some Aliens also pose as gods?</div> </div> </div> </div>SPOILERS!!!<br /> <br /> <br /> I could totally see the Doyen take that approach. It's what they did with the Chromatics, after all","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3108-malckuss","name":"Malckuss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-14T07:09:34-08:00","id":1280685,"title":"","content":"Hmm... <br /> <br /> Attitude - 1970s<br /> Avalon - Camelot<br /> Argent - post-Trinity classic scifi<br /> Atomics - post WW2 science horror adventure silliness","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-14T10:24:17-08:00","id":1280705,"title":"","content":"I'm on board for Avalon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-18T14:53:53-08:00","id":1281582,"title":"","content":"Hmm. Out in left field, AFRICA, where the only people to develop Nova powers are black. Probably too niche, but would be interesting if done intelligently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-18T15:58:58-08:00","id":1281588,"title":"","content":"My short list for divergent timeline settings...<br /> <br /> - War of the Worlds invasion actually happened in the 1890s, and the leftover tech results in the Psion age starting in the Edwardian Era!<br /> <br /> - N-Day doesn\u2019t happen, and Talents exist in a much harder sci-fi 2120s without Novas or Psions (so a possible future of contemporary Trinity Core having moved past N-Day)<br /> <br /> - Max loses and Mal succeeded in using the Trinity-test to set off N-Day in 1945 leading to a Silver Age comicbooky 1960s<br /> <br /> - a possible future of the above setting where Novas reign as god kings redesigning humanity and civilizations across the galaxy as they see fit<br /> <br /> - China goes through with their threat at the end of the Aberrant War, and a post apocalyptic Mad Max/Fallout setting results<br /> <br /> - Inspiration Age (Adventure!) never ends, and by the latter half of the 20th century democratic, communist, and fascist powers compete to spread through a pulp planetary romance solar system","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 01-18-2019, 07:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-18T16:31:31-08:00","id":1281590,"title":"","content":"I have long wanted a condensed timeline, with the Nova age starting in 1938 for a Golden Age comics/Godlike mash up in WW2, and the Psions starting in the 50s. I admit this is largely motivated by the idea of a 1962 where China is still Nationalist with telepathic ethics police to combat government corruption, the biggest cultural figure in the Middle East is Baha'i, and the most powerful person in North America is African American.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-18T18:26:16-08:00","id":1281603,"title":"","content":"&quot;- a possible future of the above setting where Novas reign as god kings redesigning humanity and civilizations across the galaxy as they see fit&quot; <br /> <br /> I would love a scifi Nova Age setting. Especially considering that novers are the ones that I love the most out of all the groups and so would like more of them. Especially a version where they don't fall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-18T18:56:03-08:00","id":1281607,"title":"","content":"A time war (my Agon idea) could link even wild alternative worlds into one system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-20T16:30:26-08:00","id":1281839,"title":"","content":"I'd love a steampunk western setting. Can't think of a good name for it, thou. <br /> <br /> Likewise a pirate setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-20T21:33:47-08:00","id":1281871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1274301-are-there-any-new-original-settings-planed-for-trinity?p=1281839#post1281839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd love a steampunk western setting. Can't think of a good name for it, thou.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you tried Deadlands?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-21T05:47:41-08:00","id":1281931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aristarkos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1274301-are-there-any-new-original-settings-planed-for-trinity?p=1281871#post1281871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Have you tried Deadlands?</div> </div> </div> </div>I had pretty much the entire run of it back during it's 1st edition, but it had a number of problems that were ultimately too personally annoying for me to overcome. Primarily was Pinnacle's &quot;everything AND the kitchen sink&quot; approach to setting design, in which it would include anything and everything even tangentially connected to the setting/genre in a giant car crash of stuff that often had little rhyme or reason. Scattering new character types (such as martial artists or practitioners of voodoo) across various sourcebooks and boxed sets was annoying, but at least no where near as bad as their superhero game which scattered the power rules themselves across various books. The fact that they tended to use really large margin spaces in their layout, padding out the page count while keeping the actually word count of written material down, was also an irritant. <br /> <br /> What I'd like for a Trinity/Adventure style western would be where something like the Hammersmith event occurs in, say, 1866 (maybe in Denver or San Fransisco) with the effects centered on the American West (say, from about the Mississippi River to the Pacific), as well as Western Canada and Northern Mexico. So you have a &quot;Wild West&quot; 1876 of cinematic gunfighters, steampunk inventors, and various other fun pulp oddities, but at a default level that's maybe an 8 out of 10 rather than Deadlands' &quot;we tried to go past 11 and now the knob is broken&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-21T07:09:49-08:00","id":1281938,"title":"","content":"Why center it in the West? Why not have it be global and have said setting include the west, so that you also have foggy Victorian Steampunk at the same time?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-21T08:10:24-08:00","id":1281949,"title":"","content":"How about the &quot;Kerberos Club&quot; setting for Wild Talents?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8890-nullapostle","name":"NullApostle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-21T13:38:54-08:00","id":1282005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1274301-are-there-any-new-original-settings-planed-for-trinity?p=1281938#post1281938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why center it in the West? Why not have it be global and have said setting include the west, so that you also have foggy Victorian Steampunk at the same time?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, partially for game focus, but I sort of have this image in my head where another Hammersmith event occurs in Europe (London or Paris maybe) which results in that region turning into a Gothic Horror-Adventure setting with some steampunk undertones (like Masque of the Red Death, but with more technology and punching) , with a third event in China turning the far East into Wuxia land. And at some point heroes of all three lands have to come together to defeat the serpent people of the hollow earth and their time traveling N-zi allies who started it all. (There might also be some sort of South Asian/Middle Eastern/East African setting, but I'm not sure what.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-21T14:10:40-08:00","id":1282010,"title":"","content":"(Total Trinity noob) What is Hammersmith event, you mention all the time?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-21T14:22:09-08:00","id":1282012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1274301-are-there-any-new-original-settings-planed-for-trinity?p=1282010#post1282010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Total Trinity noob) What is Hammersmith event, you mention all the time?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hammersmith was a scientist working on, what he calls, Z-Waves. He creates a engine capable of working this energy and on the first test it explodes, creating a wave of Noetic/Flux/Quantum wave that propagates thru the universe.<br /> The guys next to it end up dead or enhanced on overwhelming levels. This is the event that start the Adventure! Era.<br /> <br /> After that, one of the guys who was there, Divis Mal as called on Nova Era, recreate the accident, but now enhancing only quantum based superhumans, the novas, on levels that are far superior from the ones on previous eras.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-21T15:05:58-08:00","id":1282018,"title":"","content":"I'm interested, as many are, in a post-Aeon space opera setting (which I'd personally name Astral, but I think that's a highly unlikely name).<br /> <br /> I'm also interested in a post-apocalyptic setting, but I'd actually like to see it as a sequel to Aeon. I could see them as alternates (a 'dark' and 'light' sequel to Aeon), but I can also see them as two different focuses in the same time period. Maybe at some point a bunch of Abberants conquer Earth and turn it into a living hell ruled over by monstrous god-kings, but one or more of the extrasolar colonies managed to develop the technological base to create their own Jump Ships and other technology that allows them to hold off Abberant invasions, and possibly begins to have more Nova erruptions. I can even see members of the 'Galactic Nova Corps' being sent to Earth to try and free it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-21T16:59:55-08:00","id":1282036,"title":"","content":"Bruce Baugh once mentioned the concept of having a Pulp Adventure American Revolution, leading to a Steampunk Civil War and eventually a Space Opera style Great War spread throughout the Solar System, with the planets being similar to how they were imagined in Victorian, Pulp and early 50s SciFi. I'm not sure what would be the best way to do such a thing, with 20s/30s space opera, a Star Wars-esque WW2 or a Star Trek style Cold War all seeming to be equally interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-26T17:08:18-08:00","id":1282927,"title":"","content":"Hmm.<br /> <br /> <b>Apprehension: Turn of the Century Gothic Suspense and Psychic Strangeness</b><br /> <br /> In which, dear reader, during the Year of Our Lord 1898, &quot;something happens&quot;. Perhaps an experiment gone wrong, or an alien stone fallen from the sky, or an inevitable aligning of the stars, the result is our world being bathed in strange energies which have awakened psychic and occult powers across the globe. The anxieties and fears of the past, present and future are amplified, giving birth to numerous horrors, including those of fiction and folklore, sometimes overwriting the past with a secret history. This is a world of ghosts, mad scientists, and paranormal monsters, and of the psychically inspired heroes who stand against them. Inspired by the stories of Sherlock Holmes and Carnacki the Ghost Finder, as well as 19th century Gothic and turn of the century Weird Fiction, and period beliefs in psychical research and mysticism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-26T20:05:01-08:00","id":1282947,"title":"","content":"Avantguard: Space, the final frontier.<br /> <br /> The Hammersmith accident never happened, novas never erupted, Psiads are extremely rare, but the world have 1000s of Talents that developed the science faster and the colonisation of the sol system was started by mid 21st century.<br /> The year is 2323, 45 years after the creation of the warpdrive, capable of faster than light travel, the humans are living on the stars for the last 200 years, but the distances are so big the colonies out of Sol System must be fully independent. Suddenly a few dozen ships are capable of reaching the colonies in mounts instead of decades, reaching faster than the news of their creation, and the deep space exploration starts. The colonies founded over the centuries never encountered intelligent life, except for ruins of civilisations that somehow vanished long time before the colonists arrived, and the colonists were too busy to make a proper research on the subject. But now the explorers arrived, the colonies can trade and the scientists can visit this places and many more. What will they find? Doyens? Qin? Coalition? Maybe chromatic that never touched by the doyen?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 01-26-2019, 11:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-26T20:10:43-08:00","id":1282950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1274301-are-there-any-new-original-settings-planed-for-trinity?p=1282012#post1282012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hammersmith was a scientist working on, what he calls, Z-Waves. He creates a engine capable of working this energy and on the first test it explodes, creating a wave of Noetic/Flux/Quantum wave that propagates thru the universe.<br /> The guys next to it end up dead or enhanced on overwhelming levels. This is the event that start the Adventure! Era.<br /> <br /> After that, one of the guys who was there, Divis Mal as called on Nova Era, recreate the accident, but now enhancing only quantum based superhumans, the novas, on levels that are far superior from the ones on previous eras.</div> </div> </div> </div>Divas Mal\u2019s stunt created an equivalent of the Hammersmith event that was focused specifically on Quantum energies, thus the Nova era being dominated by Quantum-empowered individuals.<br /> <br /> As well, <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">another one who was empowered as what was effectively a psion Proxy later replicated the process again but with a focus on Noetics in an attempt to clean up the mess left behind by the Aberrant War, and ended up triggering the Aeon Era. The only energy type that hasn\u2019t seen a dedicated variation of the Hammersmith event is Flux. I suspect that when and if something like that happens, the result will be what I would call Travelers: individuals capable of traversing space, time, and dimension. For what it\u2019s worth, the third of the three empowered survivors of the original Hammersmith event is a Traveler.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-27T01:45:53-08:00","id":1282988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1274301-are-there-any-new-original-settings-planed-for-trinity?p=1282005#post1282005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> (There might also be some sort of South Asian/Middle Eastern/East African setting, but I'm not sure what.)</div> </div> </div> </div>It could be A Faith inspired Hammersmith event tapping into the Divine either in India or the Holy Lands. Or hell Egypt!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-27T09:32:05-08:00","id":1283067,"title":"","content":"Note that the books make it clear that \u00c6on, Aberrant, and Adventure are the only eras backed by a Hammersmith Event. All others are set in much weaker, more localized and temporary events (e.g., \u00c6gis) or in an era where the wake of any such events have largely subsided (the core book's setting, Anima). What makes these three events significant was their size and duration: all three were worldwide and in fact propagated into interstellar space; and they didn't die down naturally: the original one appears to have subsided by the time of the core book's setting only because an active effort was made to tamp down on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-27T22:12:47-08:00","id":1283195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1274301-are-there-any-new-original-settings-planed-for-trinity?p=1282010#post1282010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Total Trinity noob) What is Hammersmith event, you mention all the time?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In 1922, Doctor Sir Calvin Hammersmith invited a number of people of his acquaintance -- mostly those who were wealthy or science-minded or both -- to a demonstration of his &quot;telluric engine,&quot; which would draw energy from &quot;Z-waves,&quot; the energy of the cosmos itself. It would therefore be a potential source of limitless energy.<br /> <br /> The demonstration did not go as planned. The device exploded. Dr. Hammersmith died trying to shut it down. Those closest to the device -- in the &quot;eye&quot; of the explosion -- were imbued with a fantastic amount of Z-wave energy, what we now call Flux. Many of those attending the demonstration further away from the engine died outright.<br /> <br /> Individuals demonstrating strange and amazing powers began to manifest around the world from that point -- what some called &quot;daredevils&quot; (Talents), &quot;mesmerists&quot; (psiads), and &quot;stalwarts&quot; (novas).<br /> <br /> A year later, Maxwell Anderson Mercer and his friend Michael Donighal, who were both in the eye of the Hammersmith explosion, founded the \u00c6on Society for Gentlemen. The <b>Adventure!</b> era begins.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-27T22:37:02-08:00","id":1283204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1274301-are-there-any-new-original-settings-planed-for-trinity?p=1283195#post1283195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Individuals demonstrating strange and amazing powers began to manifest around the world from that point -- what some called &amp;quot;daredevils&amp;quot; (Talents), &amp;quot;mesmerists&amp;quot; (psiads), and &amp;quot;stalwarts&amp;quot; (novas).</div> </div> </div> </div>I was under the impression though that 2E is leaning more toward Talents always having been around. So in their case is it more that their numbers just spiked after Hammersmith, or am I wrong and the likes of Julie D\u2019Aubigny, Bass Reeves, Ching Shih, etc weren\u2019t Talents in the Continuum?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-28T10:44:36-08:00","id":1283306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1274301-are-there-any-new-original-settings-planed-for-trinity?p=1283204#post1283204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was under the impression though that 2E is leaning more toward Talents always having been around. So in their case is it more that their numbers just spiked after Hammersmith, or am I wrong and the likes of Julie D\u2019Aubigny, Bass Reeves, Ching Shih, etc weren\u2019t Talents in the Continuum?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That was also the case in 1e. We just made it more explicit in this edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-28T12:09:37-08:00","id":1283322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1274301-are-there-any-new-original-settings-planed-for-trinity?p=1282988#post1282988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It could be A Faith inspired Hammersmith event tapping into the Divine either in India or the Holy Lands. Or hell Egypt!</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking some sort of Arabian Nights inspired thing, but I'm not sure how it would work exactly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-28T13:16:46-08:00","id":1283339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1274301-are-there-any-new-original-settings-planed-for-trinity?p=1283322#post1283322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was thinking some sort of Arabian Nights inspired thing, but I'm not sure how it would work exactly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Magic magic is magic. So maybe Hammersmith event involving the Smokeless fire of the Djinn. Djinn could be high Quantum beings, aliens or even humans who lost their humanity in Quantum and reverted to a being of myth and expectation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-29T15:50:40-08:00","id":1283586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1274301-are-there-any-new-original-settings-planed-for-trinity?p=1283195#post1283195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> In 1922, Doctor Sir Calvin Hammersmith invited a number of people of his acquaintance -- mostly those who were wealthy or science-minded or both -- to a demonstration of his &amp;quot;telluric engine,&amp;quot; which would draw energy from &amp;quot;Z-waves,&amp;quot; the energy of the cosmos itself. It would therefore be a potential source of limitless energy.<br /> <br /> The demonstration did not go as planned. The device exploded. Dr. Hammersmith died trying to shut it down. Those closest to the device -- in the &amp;quot;eye&amp;quot; of the explosion -- were imbued with a fantastic amount of Z-wave energy, what we now call Flux. Many of those attending the demonstration further away from the engine died outright.<br /> <br /> Individuals demonstrating strange and amazing powers began to manifest around the world from that point -- what some called &amp;quot;daredevils&amp;quot; (Talents), &amp;quot;mesmerists&amp;quot; (psiads), and &amp;quot;stalwarts&amp;quot; (novas).<br /> <br /> A year later, Maxwell Anderson Mercer and his friend Michael Donighal, who were both in the eye of the Hammersmith explosion, founded the \u00c6on Society for Gentlemen. The <b>Adventure!</b> era begins.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you're keeping the founding of the \u00c6on Society to Max and Michael? I was figuring that that would get \u201cretconned\u201d to also include Sara. But I suppose it makes sense: she's described as preferring to work in the shadows for most of her career; so if she was involved in the founding of the \u00c6on Society, she would have kept a low profile.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-01T23:46:19-08:00","id":1284294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1274301-are-there-any-new-original-settings-planed-for-trinity?p=1283586#post1283586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So you're keeping the founding of the \u00c6on Society to Max and Michael? I was figuring that that would get \u201cretconned\u201d to also include Sara. But I suppose it makes sense: she's described as preferring to work in the shadows for most of her career; so if she was involved in the founding of the \u00c6on Society, she would have kept a low profile.</div> </div> </div> </div>She seemed to be doing her own thing, under the Radar, until she did her Psi version of the Hammersmith event in the next millennium. Perhaps Mercer knew of her from his trips to the Future but I don\u2019t believe she was in the inner echelons of the Aeon. She was probably cultivating her talents in the background, exploiting her immortality and humble origins.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-02T02:30:44-08:00","id":1284310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1274301-are-there-any-new-original-settings-planed-for-trinity?p=1284294#post1284294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> She seemed to be doing her own thing, under the Radar, until she did her Psi version of the Hammersmith event in the next millennium. Perhaps Mercer knew of her from his trips to the Future but I don\u2019t believe she was in the inner echelons of the Aeon. She was probably cultivating her talents in the background, exploiting her immortality and humble origins.</div> </div> </div> </div>Max can have invited her, but she may have refused to join Aeon Society. It would not change the fact she was not a big piece in the game until 2104.<br /> <br /> If Michael is more or less the same as in 1e, in the time he would be looking for people with powers very actively, and he could detect it without much problem. Also, he would go after her at least to talk about the experiment. This way I believe she choose to play low for a few hundred years even with some people in power knowing about her.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}